## Objective
- Passive-only security reconnaissance and vulnerability assessment of Spare's in-scope assets (api.sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com, spare.com) with continuous monitoring, hypothesis tracking, and evidence collection for bug bounty submission.

## Important Details
- **Scope (IN):** spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Scope (OUT):** ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com and spare.com; third-party services
- **Rules:** Passive-first only (GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification). Secrets as sha256 only.
- **Multi-version envoy LB** serves different code versions to fast vs slow replicas — bypasses are deterministic by replica, not probabilistic
- **Vendor patch/revert cycle observed ~2026-08-20:** fix deployed then FULLY REVERTED fleet-wide; findings are chronic not transient
- **SURVIVOR classes** (never entered patch batch): SSO oracle (`/v1/identity/workos/auth`), engage write chain (`/v1/public/engage/cases POST`), formKey oracle (`/v1/public/engage/caseForms POST`)
- **Canonical body hashes** used for reproducibility:
  - SSO oracle: `5b170be7b7829635753da63537ecfe9068be5eea0b0a6218ffd72b8770ae4414`
  - Org-key spare: `3099f1baba93ebf19434837bdd0552a72f110a262bd01528eb48e8ba71e0e8cd`
  - Regions: `27d83f3c…27b`
- **Fleet hosts:** prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat — UAT bypass parity lost (401 on all routes, removed from fleet)
- **Staging hosts** (api.staging.sparelabs.com) serve newer code with fixes prod lacks — confirms multi-version LB serves older vulnerable code
- **Forms bundle regression:** chronic across 4+ rotations (main.60865478→9f3ec6b6→7f821c2b) — contains ngrok/Atlassian/localhost refs; CA→US data routing (PIPEDA concern)
- **Platform.sparelabs.com:** CSP leak exposes admin Vercel apps (admin-eam-app, admin-fixed-route-app, prod+staging) + Metabase + 9 cloud services; no real API surface behind MFE shell
- **longcat "PATCHED" claim (2026-08-11)** on `/v1/global/regions` is confirmed FALSE POSITIVE — only tested no-auth path (400), never tested Bearer-x bypass vector

